## TLDR Problem this solves: - MLflow {{trace}} judges fail against OCI Cohere models - Tools with array-typed parameters draw an OCI 500 - The tool-result continuation turn draws an OCI 400 - Tool-grounded responses with citations fail to parse How it solves it: - Maps JSON-schema collection types to lowercase `list` / `dict` - Sends continuations as empty `message` plus top-level `toolResults` - Keeps the user turn in `chatHistory`, drops TOOL entries - Makes citation `document_ids` and search-query `generation_id` optional ## User Flow Before: a developer running an MLflow {{trace}} judge against an OCI Cohere model through the gateway sees every judge run fail 1. They send POST http://localhost:4000/v1/chat/completions for `cohere-judge` with a `get_span` tool whose `attributes_to_fetch` parameter is a JSON-schema array 2. The response is HTTP 500 wrapping OCI "Internal Server Error", so the judge never gets its first tool call 3. They retry the continuation turn, the same POST with the assistant tool call and tool result appended, and get HTTP 500 wrapping OCI 400 "cannot specify message if the last entry in chat history contains tool results" 4. The judge aborts and the trace gets no score After: the same requests complete and the judge scores the trace 1. They send the same POST http://localhost:4000/v1/chat/completions with the array-typed tool parameter 2. HTTP 200 comes back with a `get_span` entry in `tool_calls` 3. They append the assistant tool call and tool result and POST again 4. HTTP 200 comes back with the grounded answer ("There are 47 spans in the trace.") and real token usage ## Relevant issues Re-lands #30646, which was rolled back in a batch stabilization revert (commit `15a7c687`) along with several unrelated PRs. The greptile-review hardening applied on top of the original merge is folded in. A user in this PR's thread is currently blocked on this fix for their OCI GenAI deployment and independently verified the top-level `toolResults` request shape against the raw OCI API The three underlying bugs, all hit by judges that send tools and run an agentic tool-calling loop: 1. Tool parameter types: a JSON-schema `array` parameter mapped to the bare string `"List"`, which OCI's Cohere backend rejects with a 500. The mapping now emits the lowercase builtins `list` / `dict` 2. Continuation turns: litellm pulled the last user message into the top-level `message` and emitted the tool result as a TOOL entry in `chatHistory`, which OCI rejects. OCI carries the current turn's results in a dedicated top-level `toolResults` field, so the transform now sends an empty `message`, keeps the user turn in `chatHistory`, and puts results in `toolResults`, matching the langchain-oracle reference 3. Response parsing: tool-grounded answers return citations carrying `documentIds` and no `document_ids`, which sank the whole parse because `CohereCitation.document_ids` was required. That field and `CohereSearchQuery.generation_id` are now optional Latest push rebases onto the current `litellm_internal_staging` tip (`d5b91b94d3`) and renames one cross-module helper to stay under the basedpyright private-usage budget, with no semantic changes. Verified locally at the new tip: `ruff format --check` clean, all three budget gates pass, the OCI unit suite passes (372 tests), and the four gated live Cohere tool integration tests pass against real OCI GenAI ## Linear ticket ## Pre-Submission checklist **Please complete all items before asking a LiteLLM maintainer to review your PR** - [x] I have added meaningful tests - [x] My PR passes all CI/CD checks (e.g., lint, format, unit tests) - [x] My PR's scope is as isolated as possible; it only solves 1 specific problem - [x] I have received a Greptile **Confidence Score of at least 4/5** before requesting a maintainer review (Greptile reviews automatically once the PR is opened; only comment `@greptileai` to re-request a review after pushing changes) ## Delays in PR merge? If you're seeing 