## TLDR Problem this solves: - Bedrock managed batches could not be cancelled through the proxy - `POST /v1/batches/{id}/cancel` returned 400 without reaching AWS - The Bedrock job kept running and billing to completion How it solves it: - Batch cancel now calls Bedrock `StopModelInvocationJob` - Returns the refreshed job status after stopping - Maps `Stopping` to `cancelling` and `Stopped` to `cancelled` - Cancelling an already finished job returns its terminal status - Genuine stop failures still raise instead of being swallowed ## User Flow Before: the cancel call is rejected by the gateway, and the Bedrock job keeps running and billing to completion 1. An operator uploads a 100-record JSONL with POST https://litellm-domain/v1/files (multipart: `purpose=batch`, `target_model_names=bedrock-batch-haiku`, the file) and gets back a long scrambled managed file id 2. They start the batch with POST https://litellm-domain/v1/batches sending `{"input_file_id": "<that id>", "endpoint": "/v1/chat/completions", "completion_window": "24h"}` and get a batch id with `"status": "validating"` 3. They realize the batch was submitted by mistake and call POST https://litellm-domain/v1/batches/{batch_id}/cancel 4. The call fails with HTTP 400: `LiteLLM doesn't support bedrock for 'cancel_batch'. Only 'openai', 'azure', and 'vertex_ai' are supported.` 5. GET https://litellm-domain/v1/batches/{batch_id} keeps showing `"status": "in_progress"` until the job finishes, and every record is billed After: the same cancel call stops the job at AWS, and the batch reports cancelling, then cancelled 1. An operator uploads a 100-record JSONL with POST https://litellm-domain/v1/files (multipart: `purpose=batch`, `target_model_names=bedrock-batch-haiku`, the file) and gets back a long scrambled managed file id 2. They start the batch with POST https://litellm-domain/v1/batches sending `{"input_file_id": "<that id>", "endpoint": "/v1/chat/completions", "completion_window": "24h"}` and get a batch id with `"status": "validating"` 3. They realize the batch was submitted by mistake and call POST https://litellm-domain/v1/batches/{batch_id}/cancel 4. The call returns HTTP 200 with the batch showing `"status": "cancelling"` 5. GET https://litellm-domain/v1/batches/{batch_id} soon shows `"status": "cancelled"`, and the job has stopped at AWS ## Relevant issues Fixes #33986 ## Linear ticket Resolves LIT-4854 ## Pre-Submission checklist **Please complete all items before asking a LiteLLM maintainer to review your PR** - [x] I have added meaningful tests - [x] My PR passes all CI/CD checks (e.g., lint, format, unit tests) - [x] My PR's scope is as isolated as possible; it only solves 1 specific problem - [x] I have received a Greptile **Confidence Score of at least 4/5** before requesting a maintainer review (Greptile reviews automatically once the PR is opened; only comment `@greptileai` to re-request a review after pushing changes) ## Delays in PR merge? If you're seeing a delay in your PR being merged, ping the LiteLLM Team on [Slack (#pr-review)](https://join.slack.com/t/litellmossslack/shared_invite/zt-3o7nkuyfr-p_kbNJj8taRfXGgQI1~YyA). ## Screenshots / Proof of Fix Live proxy plus real AWS Bedrock model invocation jobs (us-west-2, `bedrock/us.anthropic.claude-haiku-4-5-20251001-v1:0`, managed file with `target_model_names`), no mocks. Each leg uploads a 100-record JSONL, creates a batch, then cancels it through the proxy ### Before, at base `91aee78e78`: cancel is rejected and the AWS job keeps running ``` $ curl -sS http://localhost:41837/v1/files -H "Authorization: Bearer sk-qa-***" \ -F purpose=batch -F target_model_names=bedrock-batch-haiku -F file=@batch_input.jsonl {"id":"bGl0ZWxsbV9wcm94eTphcHBsaWNhdGlvbi9vY3RldC1zdHJlYW07...NGIzNw","object":"file","purpose":"batch","status":"uploaded",...} $ curl -sS -X POST http://localhost:41837/v1/batches -H "Authorization: Bearer sk-qa-***" \ -H "Content-Type: application/json" \ -d '{"input_file_id": "<file_id>", "en