## TLDR Problem this solves: - /v1/ocr only returns LiteLLM's normalized OCR shape - Azure Document Intelligence callers need its own `analyzeResult` - switching to passthrough loses per page cost tracking How it solves it: - opt in with `x-req-format: native` (or body `req_format`) - Azure's completed operation JSON is returned untouched - normalized parsing still runs, so pages are still billed - default stays the normalized LiteLLM OCR schema - invalid or unsupported `req_format` requests fail fast with 400 ## User Flow Before: a developer parsing Azure Document Intelligence output through the gateway cannot get Azure's own payload, so their existing Azure SDK parsing code has nothing to read 1. They send POST https://litellm-domain/v1/ocr with `{"model": "azure-doc-intelligence", "document": {...}}` and the header `x-req-format: native` 2. The header is ignored and the 200 response is LiteLLM's own shape: `pages[].markdown`, `pages[].dimensions`, `usage_info`, with no `status`, no `analyzeResult`, no `words`, `lines`, `paragraphs`, `spans` or `angle` 3. Their only way to get Azure's shape is the passthrough route, which drops the page based spend they rely on After: the same request returns Azure's raw completed operation, and spend is still recorded 1. They send the same POST https://litellm-domain/v1/ocr with `x-req-format: native` 2. The 200 response is Azure's own payload: `status: "succeeded"`, `createdDateTime`, `lastUpdatedDateTime`, and the full `analyzeResult` with `content`, `pages[].words`, `pages[].lines`, `pages[].spans`, `pages[].angle`, `paragraphs`, `tables` and `sections` 3. The response still carries `x-litellm-response-cost`, so the request is charged per page exactly as before 4. Sending the same request without the header, or with `x-req-format: litellm`, returns the unchanged normalized LiteLLM response 5. An unknown value, in the header or in the body, comes back as 400 naming the allowed values 6. Asking a model without native support (e.g. Mistral OCR) for `native` comes back as 400 naming the provider, instead of silently ignoring the request or erroring with 500 ## Relevant issues ## Linear ticket Resolves LIT-5645 ## Pre-Submission checklist **Please complete all items before asking a LiteLLM maintainer to review your PR** - [x] I have added meaningful tests - [x] My PR passes all CI/CD checks (e.g., lint, format, unit tests) - [x] My PR's scope is as isolated as possible; it only solves 1 specific problem - [x] I have received a Greptile **Confidence Score of at least 4/5** before requesting a maintainer review (Greptile reviews automatically once the PR is opened; only comment `@greptileai` to re-request a review after pushing changes) ## Screenshots / Proof of Fix Shared setup, live proxy against real Azure Document Intelligence (`prebuilt-layout`, api version 2024-11-30): ```bash cat > ocr_proof_config.yaml <<'EOF' model_list: - model_name: azure-doc-intelligence litellm_params: model: azure_ai/doc-intelligence/prebuilt-layout api_base: os.environ/AZURE_DOCUMENT_INTELLIGENCE_ENDPOINT api_key: os.environ/AZURE_DOCUMENT_INTELLIGENCE_API_KEY - model_name: mistral-ocr litellm_params: model: mistral/mistral-ocr-latest api_key: fake-key general_settings: master_key: sk-1234 EOF cat > ocr_payload.json <<'EOF' { "model": "azure-doc-intelligence", "document": { "type": "document_url", "document_url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Azure-Samples/cognitive-services-REST-api-samples/master/curl/form-recognizer/sample-layout.pdf" } } EOF python litellm/proxy/proxy_cli.py --config ocr_proof_config.yaml --port 4000 ``` ### Before (9d40cd4df7) #### native format requested 1. Request: ```bash curl -s -D h.txt -X POST http://localhost:4000/v1/ocr \ -H "Authorization: Bearer sk-1234" -H "Content-Type: application/json" \ -H "x-req-format: native" -d @ocr_payload.json -o r.json grep -i '^x-litellm-response-cost:' h.txt python3 -c "import json;d=json.load(open('r.json'));print(sorted(d.keys()));print('has analyzeResult:', 'analyzeResult' in d);print('page0 keys', sorted(d['pages'][0].keys()));print('usage_info', d['usage_info'])" ``` 2. Output, header ignored, Azure's payload unavailable: ``` x-litellm-response-cost: 0.01 ['content', 'document_annotation', 'keyValuePairs', 'model', 'object', 'pages', 'tables', 'usage_info'] has analyzeResult: False page0 keys ['dimensions', 'images', 'index', 'markdown'] usage_info {'pages_processed': 1, 'credits': None, 'doc_size_bytes': None} ``` #### unknown format requested 1. Request: ```bash curl -s -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code}
