## TLDR Problem this solves: - POST /v1/batches with a string `metadata` returned 200 and silently dropped it - A string `litellm_metadata` returned 500 `'str' object has no attribute 'update'` - Numbers and lists in either field also surfaced as 500s - The same bad values 500'd /v1/responses and /v1/messages too - OpenAI returns 400 for every non-object metadata value How it solves it: - Non-object `metadata` / `litellm_metadata` now get a 400 naming the field and received type - JSON strings that parse to an object still work (multipart/form-data and extra_body callers need this) - Every invalid value is dropped before raising so failure logging can't mask the 400 as a 500 - /v1/messages and /v1/moderations re-raise ProxyException as-is instead of wrapping into a 500 ## User Flow Before: a team tagging each batch with a cost centre receives 200 and the tag is absent from the batch 1. They send POST https://litellm-domain/v1/files with `purpose=batch` and their JSONL, and receive a file ID 2. They send POST https://litellm-domain/v1/batches with `"metadata": "cost-centre=research"`; the response is 200 carrying a batch ID and `"metadata": null` 3. They send GET https://litellm-domain/v1/batches/{batch_id} and the response still reports `"metadata": null`, so the tag is gone 4. A colleague sends the create with `"litellm_metadata": "abc"` and receives 500 with `'str' object has no attribute 'update'` 5. Another teammate sends `"metadata": 42` and receives 500 with `'int' object has no attribute 'get'` After: any non-object value gets a 400 naming the field and its type, and object tags survive end to end 1. They send POST https://litellm-domain/v1/files with `purpose=batch` and their JSONL, and receive a file ID 2. The same POST https://litellm-domain/v1/batches with `"metadata": "cost-centre=research"` returns 400 with `Invalid type for 'metadata': expected an object, but got a string instead.` and `"param": "metadata"` 3. They resend with `"metadata": {"cost_centre": "research"}` (or that object serialised as a JSON string); the response is 200 and carries `"metadata": {"cost_centre": "research"}` 4. GET https://litellm-domain/v1/batches/{batch_id} reports `"metadata": {"cost_centre": "research"}` 5. The colleague's `"litellm_metadata": "abc"` create returns 400 with `Invalid type for 'litellm_metadata': expected an object, but got a string instead.` and `"param": "litellm_metadata"` 6. The teammate's `"metadata": 42` create returns 400 with `Invalid type for 'metadata': expected an object, but got an integer instead.` and `"param": "metadata"` ## Relevant issues Fixes #37147 ## Linear ticket Resolves LIT-5658 ## Pre-Submission checklist **Please complete all items before asking a LiteLLM maintainer to review your PR** - [x] I have added meaningful tests - [x] My PR passes all CI/CD checks (e.g., lint, format, unit tests) - [x] My PR's scope is as isolated as possible; it only solves 1 specific problem - [x] I have received a Greptile **Confidence Score of at least 4/5** before requesting a maintainer review (Greptile reviews automatically once the PR is opened; only comment `@greptileai` to re-request a review after pushing changes) ## Delays in PR merge? If you're seeing a delay in your PR being merged, ping the LiteLLM Team on [Slack (#pr-review)](https://join.slack.com/t/litellmossslack/shared_invite/zt-3o7nkuyfr-p_kbNJj8taRfXGgQI1~YyA). ## Screenshots / Proof of Fix Both legs ran the identical script against a live proxy hitting the real OpenAI API: the before leg from a worktree at the merge base, the after leg from the PR branch tip. Shared setup per leg: model_list entries `gpt-5-batch` -> `openai/gpt-5.6` and `moderation-check` -> `openai/omni-moderation-latest`, master key, Postgres `database_url`, one JSONL upload ``` printf '%s
