## TLDR Problem this solves: - Gemini 3 detection matched the substring "gemini-3" - It misses `gemini-flash-latest`, which resolves to Gemini 3.x - It will also miss `gemini-4-*` once Google ships it - Tool-call replay on those names fails with `400 missing a thought_signature` How it solves it: - Read the major version off the name, compare against 3 - Match the three unversioned rolling aliases by exact name ## User Flow Before: a developer whose agent calls a tool, then replays the result, gets a 400 on the follow-up turn, so the agent loop dies after its first tool call 1. They send `POST http://localhost:4000/v1/chat/completions` with `"model": "gemini/gemini-flash-latest"`, a `search_website` tool, and one user message 2. The reply contains a tool call, so they run their tool and collect the result 3. They send the same route the full history: the user message, the assistant tool call stored under their own id `call_abc123`, and a `role: "tool"` result 4. The response is `400`, reading `Function call is missing a thought_signature in functionCall parts. This is required for tools to work correctly` 5. Sending the identical history with `"model": "gemini/gemini-3.5-flash"` returns `200`, so the failure looks specific to the alias After: the same replay returns an answer, so the agent loop continues past its first tool call 1. They send `POST http://localhost:4000/v1/chat/completions` with `"model": "gemini/gemini-flash-latest"`, a `search_website` tool, and one user message 2. The reply contains a tool call, so they run their tool and collect the result 3. They send the same route the full history: the user message, the assistant tool call stored under their own id `call_abc123`, and a `role: "tool"` result 4. The response is `200`, carrying the assistant's answer summarising the tool result 5. `"model": "gemini/gemini-3.5-flash"` still returns `200`, exactly as it did before ## Relevant issues Related to #25322, where the reported `400 ... missing a thought_signature` comes from the same code path. This PR covers the case where the model's generation is not recognised from its name, and does not change signature propagation from thought parts ## Linear ticket ## Pre-Submission checklist - [x] I have added meaningful tests - [x] My PR passes all CI/CD checks (e.g., lint, format, unit tests) - [x] My PR's scope is as isolated as possible; it only solves 1 specific problem - [x] I have received a Greptile **Confidence Score of at least 4/5** before requesting a maintainer review (Greptile reviews automatically once the PR is opened; only comment `@greptileai` to re-request a review after pushing changes) ## Screenshots / Proof of Fix Real calls to the Google AI Studio API through a live proxy, no mocks. Both runs use this setup unchanged: ```bash cat > config.yaml <<'YAML' model_list: - model_name: gemini/gemini-flash-latest litellm_params: model: gemini/gemini-flash-latest api_key: os.environ/GEMINI_API_KEY - model_name: gemini/gemini-3.5-flash litellm_params: model: gemini/gemini-3.5-flash api_key: os.environ/GEMINI_API_KEY - model_name: gemini/gemini-3.7-flash litellm_params: model: gemini/gemini-3.7-flash api_key: os.environ/GEMINI_API_KEY general_settings: master_key: sk-1234 YAML cat > payload.json <<'JSON' { "model": "gemini/gemini-flash-latest", "messages": [ {"role": "user", "content": "What trips do you have to Iceland? Use the tool."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": null, "tool_calls": [ {"id": "call_abc123", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "search_website", "arguments": "{"query": "Iceland"}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "call_abc123", "content": "[{"title": "Iceland Highlands Trek", "price": "EUR 2400"}]"} ], "tools": [{"type": "function", "function": { "name": "search_website", "description": "Search the client website", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"query": {"type": "string"}}, "required": ["query"]}}}] } JSON ``` The assistant tool call carries a plain client-side id with no `__thought__` signature attached, which is what a client that stores tool calls under its own ids replays. The two explicitly versioned models act as the control: they are already detected correctly, so they must be unaffected ### Before (973329e) #### the rolling alias 1. `python litellm/proxy/proxy_cli.py --config config.yaml --port 4000` 2. `curl -s -w "
HTTP %{http_code}
